      <p>Government offices, courier depots, universities, and commercial areas generate the most tasks. Position yourself near these locations during peak hours (9 AM - 1 PM, 3 PM - 6 PM).</p>
      <h2>Earning Potential</h2>
      <p>Average task: ₹200-500. Completing 5-10 tasks daily puts you at ₹1000-5000. Top helpers earn ₹3000+ on busy days.</p>
    `,
  },
  "safety-tips-for-helpers": {
    title: "Safety Tips: What Every Helper Should Know Before Claiming a Task",
    date: "2026-06-10",
    category: "Trust & Safety",
    content: `
      <p>Your safety comes first. Follow these guidelines when completing tasks for strangers.</p>
      <h2>Before Claiming</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Check the poster's profile — look for verified badge, ratings, and task history</li>
        <li>Read the full task description carefully</li>
        <li>If something feels off, don't claim it. Report it instead.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>During the Task</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep all communication within the StrangerHelp chat (it's logged)</li>
        <li>Never share personal details like home address or bank PIN</li>
        <li>Take photos of everything — they serve as your proof</li>
        <li>If asked to do something illegal or uncomfortable, cancel and report</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Payment Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Confirm payment method before starting work</li>
        <li>For UPI payments, verify you received the money before marking complete</li>
        <li>Never accept checks or "pay later" promises</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Red Flags to Watch For</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Tasks that ask you to receive/send money on someone's behalf</li>
        <li>Requests to meet at isolated locations at odd hours</li>
        <li>Posters who refuse to communicate via chat</li>
        <li>Tasks that seem too good to be true (very high pay for minimal work)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>When in doubt, trust your instincts and report suspicious activity.</p>
    `,
  },
  "building-strangerhelp": {
    title: "Building StrangerHelp: From Idea to India's First Hyperlocal Task Network",
    date: "2026-06-08",
    category: "Company",
    content: `
      <p>StrangerHelp started with a simple frustration: needing to submit a document at a government office 20km away, knowing someone nearby could do it in 5 minutes.</p>
      <h2>The Problem</h2>
      <p>India runs on physical presence. Despite digitization, millions of tasks still require someone to physically be somewhere — collect a receipt, verify a property, stand in a queue, pick up a parcel. Most people can't always be where they need to be.</p>
      <h2>The Insight</h2>
      <p>At any given moment, there are people near those locations who have free time and would happily earn ₹200-500 for 15 minutes of work. The connection was missing.</p>
      <h2>What We've Built</h2>
      <p>StrangerHelp connects these two groups through:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A location-aware task marketplace</li>
        <li>Real-time helper availability (Pulse map)</li>
        <li>Trust infrastructure (verification, karma, reviews)</li>
        <li>Instant messaging between poster and helper</li>
        <li>Photo-proof completion system</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What's Next</h2>
      <p>We're building escrow payments (Karma Wallet), expanding to more cities, and adding features like task chaining and voice task posting. Our goal: make "getting things done" as easy as sending a message.</p>
      <p>If you believe in what we're building, <a href="/tasks/new">post your first task</a> or <a href="/register">sign up as a helper</a> today.</p>
    `,
  },
  "voice-task-posting": {
    title: "Voice Task Posting: Just Speak and Your Task is Live",
    date: "2026-06-25",
